---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Build the folder into an output folder and print its deploy id.

Usage: ink build [OPTIONS]

Also typed as ink b

Examples
  ink build                      # Build this folder into .ink/out
  ink build --strict             # The same, but a warning stops the build
  ink -C garden build -o public  # Build another folder into ./public

Output
  -o, --out <DIR>   Where to write the site [default: .ink/out]
      --base <URL>  The address the site is served at, for feeds and canonical
                    links
      --strict      Exit 6 on warnings, and write nothing

Work
      --cache <DIR>  Where to keep work between builds, such as image copies
                     [default: .ink/cache]

Source
      --source <KIND>  `folder` reads the files on disk, `git` reads a commit
                       [default: `git` when .git exists, said as a notice]
      --rev <REV>      The commit to read, as `git rev-parse` takes it; only for
                       a git repository [default: HEAD]

Verification
      --check             Build natively and through the wasm components, write
                          nothing, and fail (exit 1) when the two deploys differ
      --components <DIR>  A folder whose components replace the ones `ink`
                          carries when `--check` runs them:
                          `format-markdown.wasm` (or `format-obsidian.wasm` for
                          a vault) and `theme-quiet.wasm`, as `cargo xtask
                          component` writes them. A file the folder lacks is the
                          bundled one; each component run says which it used
                          (`-v`, or `components` in `--json`). Compiled
                          components are kept in `components/` of the cache

Notes
  The folder is read, interpreted and rendered in full before the output folder
  is touched. A build that fails, or warns under --strict, writes nothing: the
  previous build stays as it was.

Exit codes
  0  Built; warnings, if any, were printed
  1  The site has errors, or --check found the two builds differ; nothing was
     written
  2  Wrong usage, or an output folder ink will not write into; nothing was
     changed
  6  --strict was given and there were warnings; nothing was written

See also  ink check, ink serve, ink push
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
          (see `ink --help`)
